<title>TURKEY: TURK TUBORG H1 NET PROFIT RISES.</title>
<headline>TURK TUBORG H1 NET PROFIT RISES.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)    37.70  vs     265.37</p>
<p>    Net profit		     56.58  vs	26.55</p>
<p>    Net sales		   2,685.37  vs   1,604.99</p>
<p>    Operating loss		135.63  vs     122.45 profit</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	1,285.02  vs     411.40</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	 121.40  vs	74.94</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 945.58  vs     447.44</p>
<p>    Total debts		 5,526.84  vs   2,969.07</p>
<p>    Equity			3,687.90  vs   1,871.27</p>
<p>    Capital		     1,500.75  vs     100.05</p>
<p>NOTE - Brewer, malt and beverage producer Turk Tuborg Bira ve Malt Sanayii A.S. whose shares are also listed on the Stuttgart bourse, is owned 52.57 percent by Aegean-based food and paint group Yasar Holding.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>The company recently said it planned to double its capital to 3,001.5 billion lira by issuing 0.1 right and 0.9 bonus for one existing share after securing approval from the regulatory Capital Markets Board (SPK). -- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
